# Cursor Editor — Workspace Trust Model

## Overview

Cursor inherits VS Code's workspace trust system, which controls which features and capabilities are available based on whether the current workspace is trusted. This security model prevents unauthorized code execution and protects against malicious project configurations.

---

## What Is Workspace Trust?

Workspace trust is a security model that determines whether Cursor should allow potentially dangerous operations in a given project. It is especially important when opening workspaces from unknown or untrusted sources.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Open workspace] --> B{Is workspace trusted?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Full trust mode]
    B -->|No| D[Restricted trust mode]
    
    C --> E[All features available]
    C --> F[Agent can execute Shell]
    C --> F[Agent can run Task]
    C --> F[Agent can use CallMcpTool]
    C --> F[Hooks execute automatically]
    
    D --> G[Restricted features]
    D --> H[Agent cannot execute Shell]
    D --> H[Agent cannot run Task]
    D --> H[Agent cannot use CallMcpTool]
    D --> H[Hooks do not execute]
    D --> I[Read-only agent operations]
```

---

## Trusted vs Untrusted Workspaces

### Feature Availability by Trust Level

| Feature | Trusted | Untrusted | Notes |
|---------|---------|-----------|-------|
| **File read/write** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | Always available |
| **Grep/Search** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | Always available |
| **Shell execution** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | Dangerous operation |
| **Task (subagent)** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | May execute commands |
| **CallMcpTool** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | MCP tools may execute |
| **Hooks** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | May trigger commands |
| **Automations** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | Cloud agent may execute |
| **Web search/fetch** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | Read-only operations |
| **Semantic search** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | Read-only operations |
| **Git operations** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Limited | Read git status only |
| **Settings access** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Limited | Some settings hidden |
| **Agent Output channel** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Limited | Reduced visibility |

### Trust Impact on Agent Behavior

```
Untrusted Workspace — Agent Behavior:
  ✅ Can: Read files, grep, search, explain, suggest
  ❌ Cannot: Execute shell commands, modify settings, run hooks
  ⚠️  Result: Agent acts in Ask/Plan mode only
  
Trusted Workspace — Agent Behavior:
  ✅ Can: Everything (including Shell, Task, MCP)
  ⚠️  Result: Full Agent mode available
```

