## How Trust Affects Agent Behavior

### Agent Mode Restrictions in Untrusted Workspaces

| Agent Capability | Untrusted Workspace | Trusted Workspace |
|-----------------|---------------------|-------------------|
| **Read files** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| **Grep/Search** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| **Write files** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| **StrReplace** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| **Shell commands** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| **Spawn Task subagent** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| **Execute hooks** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| **Run Automations** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| **Access MCP tools** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| **Git operations (write)** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| **Commit changes** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |

### Practical Impact

```
Scenario: Agent needs to run tests

Untrusted workspace:
  Agent: "I can see the test files and explain what they do,
         but I cannot run 'npm test' because Shell execution
         is blocked in this untrusted workspace."
  
Trusted workspace:
  Agent: "Running npm test... Tests passing: 42/42."
```

