## How to Grant Trust

### UI Controls

```
1. Open workspace in Cursor
2. If untrusted, notification appears: "This workspace is not trusted"
3. Click "Trust workspace" button in notification
4. OR: Command Palette → "Developer: Trust Workspace"
5. OR: Status bar → Click trust indicator → "Trust workspace"
```

### Trust Levels

| Trust Level | Features Available | Scope |
|------------|-------------------|-------|
| **No trust** | Read-only agent, file ops, search | Restricted |
| **Partial trust** | Most features except shell/automation | Configurable |
| **Full trust** | All features available | Full access |

### Trust Persistence

| Trust Type | Scope | Persistence |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| **Per-workspace trust** | Specific folder | Saves to `.vscode/workspace trust` |
| **Per-folder trust** | Specific folder path | Persists across sessions |
| **Global trust** | All workspaces | Not recommended |
| **Temporary trust** | Current session only | Resets on close |

### Trust Configuration

```json
{
  // Trust configuration (in workspace settings)
  "security.workspace.trust.enabled": true,
  "security.workspace.trust.untrustedFiles": "prompt",
  
  // Trust options: "prompt" | "open" | "newWindow"
  "security.workspace.trust.onStart": "prompt",
  
  // Trusted folders (explicitly trusted)
  "security.workspace.trust.trustedFolders": [
    "/path/to/project-a",
    "/path/to/project-b"
  ],
  
  // Untrusted folders (explicitly restricted)
  "security.workspace.trust.untrustedFolders": [
    "/path/to/untrusted-project"
  ]
}
```

