## Trust and Specific Operations

### Shell Command Trust

Shell commands require full trust because they can execute arbitrary system commands:

```json
{
  // Agent can execute shell commands in trusted workspace only
  "cursor.agent.shell.enabled": true,
  "cursor.agent.shell.trustRequired": true
}
```

### Hook Execution Trust

Cursor hooks (automations) require trust because they can run on workspace events:

```
Untrusted workspace:
  - Pre-open hooks: Skipped
  - Pre-tool-use hooks: Skipped
  - Post-tool hooks: Skipped
  
Trusted workspace:
  - All hooks execute as configured
```

### MCP Tool Trust

MCP tools can interact with external systems and require trust:

```
Untrusted workspace:
  - CallMcpTool: ❌ Blocked
  
Trusted workspace:
  - CallMcpTool: ✅ Allowed
```

### Git Operation Trust

```
Untrusted workspace:
  - git status: ✅ Allowed (read)
  - git diff: ✅ Allowed (read)
  - git add: ❌ Blocked
  - git commit: ❌ Blocked
  - git push: ❌ Blocked
  - git branch: ❌ Blocked
```

